// F68: a `#[deprecated]` use is reported on an ordinary compile, with no `--lint` anywhere -- which
// is the whole point of the change, since a warning that needs a second command is one almost
// nobody sees. The two older fixtures (`lint_deprecated_cross_module`,
// `lint_deprecated_type_cross_module`) still pass `--lint` and still assert that it reports these
// too and exits 1; this one asserts that the flag is no longer what makes them appear.
//
// It also pins the part that makes the change safe: the program **type-checks and runs**, printing
// its answer and exiting 0. A warning is not an error, so turning this on cannot break a build that
// was passing -- which is why there is a `.exit` of 0 beside the `.diag`.
use oldlib

fn main() {
    print(oldlib.twice(5))
    print(oldlib.doubled(5))
    print(oldlib.quadrupled(1))
}
